IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lsl-dates`
IMPORT `lsl-employee`

-- Long Service Leave Act 1976 (ACT) -- worked cases for the questions of the employee.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL, except
-- the Act's own example in s 2G (Fiona), which is asserted as the Act states it.
--
-- (c) Australian Capital Territory. Used under CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Unofficial text.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Short names`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`on` d m y MEANS `the calendar date` d m y

`ANY DAY` MEANS `on` 1 1 2000

`DISPUTE` MEANS `an industrial dispute (a strike or lockout)`
`STOOD DOWN` MEANS `being stood down by my employer because of slackness of trade`
`OTHER BREAK` MEANS `any other break, including my resigning or my employer ending my service`

`KEPT, COUNTS` MEANS `continuity kept, and the time counts as service (dictionary, continuous service, or s 2G (2) (f) or (g))`
`KEPT, NOT COUNTED` MEANS `continuity kept, but the time of the break is not counted as service (s 2G (2) or (3), and s 2G (5))`
`KEPT, 2 WEEKS COUNT` MEANS `continuity kept: up to 2 weeks of illness or injury leave in the year counts as service; the rest is leave with your employer's permission, not counted (dictionary, continuous service (b); s 2G (2) (c), (5))`
`BROKEN` MEANS `continuity broken: you did not return within the time s 2G allows, so no head of s 2G (2) or (3) saves the break (the text's no)`
`NOT KNOWN YET` MEANS `not known yet: you have not returned, and the time s 2G allows for your return has not run out`

`ILLNESS` MEANS `I resigned because of illness or incapacity`
`NECESSITY` MEANS `I resigned because of a domestic or other pressing necessity`
`OTHER REASON` MEANS `I resigned or retired for another reason`
`DIED` MEANS `I died (the claim is by my legal personal representative)`
`DISMISSED` MEANS `my employer ended it`

`FT` MEANS `full-time at the end`
`PT` MEANS `part-time or casual at the end`

`PRO RATA YES` MEANS `yes: you had at least 5 but less than 7 years of service, and the employment ended in one of the ways s 11C (1) (a) lists (s 11C (1))`
`PRO RATA NOT A LISTED WAY` MEANS `no: the employment did not end in one of the ways s 11C (1) (a) lists (the text's no, s 11C (1) (a))`

§ `Dictionary -- employee`

#ASSERT `dictionary -- am I an employee for this Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you are an employee for this Act (dictionary, employee; s 2C for commission)`
#ASSERT `dictionary -- am I an employee for this Act` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: a public employee is not an employee for this Act (the text's no, dictionary, employee (b) (i))`
#ASSERT `dictionary -- am I an employee for this Act` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: a person employed by a member of the Legislative Assembly under the Legislative Assembly (Members' Staff) Act 1989, s 10, is not an employee for this Act (the text's no, dictionary, employee (b) (ii))`
#ASSERT `dictionary -- am I an employee for this Act` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Act does not define who is employed; on these facts you are not employed by anyone, and the Act says nothing more (NOTHING-kind)`

§ `Dictionary -- ordinary remuneration; s 2F commission`

-- Wages 1,000 + skill 50 + board and lodging allowance 30 + usual bonus 20 + board and lodging provided 100 = 1,200.
#ASSERT `dictionary -- my ordinary remuneration for a week` 1000 50 30 20 100 EQUALS 1200
#ASSERT `dictionary -- my ordinary remuneration for a week` 1000 0 0 0 0 EQUALS 1000
-- s 2F: 52,000 / 52 = 1,000; 78,000 / 52 = 1,500.
#ASSERT `s 2F -- my weekly salary or wages when paid by commission` 52000 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `s 2F -- my weekly salary or wages when paid by commission` 78000 EQUALS 1500

§ `s 2G -- breaks in service`

-- Industrial dispute, back on the settlement terms (Fiona's strike, 1 June to 30 September 1995).
#ASSERT `s 2G -- what does this break do to my service` `DISPUTE` TRUE 0 (`on` 1 6 1995) TRUE (`on` 1 10 1995) (`on` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `KEPT, NOT COUNTED`
-- Dispute, not yet back: the s 2G (2) (a) return may still come.
#ASSERT `s 2G -- what does this break do to my service` `DISPUTE` FALSE 0 (`on` 1 6 2026) FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 1 9 2026) EQUALS `NOT KNOWN YET`
-- Dispute, back but not on settlement terms: falls to s 2G (2) (e). 2 months after 1 June 2026 is 1 August 2026.
#ASSERT `s 2G -- what does this break do to my service` `DISPUTE` FALSE 0 (`on` 1 6 2026) TRUE (`on` 1 8 2026) (`on` 1 9 2026) EQUALS `KEPT, NOT COUNTED`
#ASSERT `s 2G -- what does this break do to my service` `DISPUTE` FALSE 0 (`on` 1 6 2026) TRUE (`on` 2 8 2026) (`on` 1 9 2026) EQUALS `BROKEN`
-- Stood down 31 August 2026: 6 months after is 28 February 2027 (no 31 February).
#ASSERT `s 2G -- what does this break do to my service` `STOOD DOWN` FALSE 0 (`on` 31 8 2026) TRUE (`on` 28 2 2027) (`on` 1 4 2027) EQUALS `KEPT, NOT COUNTED`
#ASSERT `s 2G -- what does this break do to my service` `STOOD DOWN` FALSE 0 (`on` 31 8 2026) TRUE (`on` 1 3 2027) (`on` 1 4 2027) EQUALS `BROKEN`
#ASSERT `s 2G -- what does this break do to my service` `STOOD DOWN` FALSE 0 (`on` 31 8 2026) FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 28 2 2027) EQUALS `NOT KNOWN YET`
#ASSERT `s 2G -- what does this break do to my service` `STOOD DOWN` FALSE 0 (`on` 31 8 2026) FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `BROKEN`
-- Leave.
#ASSERT `s 2G -- what does this break do to my service` `annual leave or long service leave` FALSE 0 `ANY DAY` TRUE `ANY DAY` `ANY DAY` EQUALS `KEPT, COUNTS`
#ASSERT `s 2G -- what does this break do to my service` `leave because of illness or injury not arising from my work` FALSE 14 `ANY DAY` TRUE `ANY DAY` `ANY DAY` EQUALS `KEPT, COUNTS`
#ASSERT `s 2G -- what does this break do to my service` `leave because of illness or injury not arising from my work` FALSE 15 `ANY DAY` TRUE `ANY DAY` `ANY DAY` EQUALS `KEPT, 2 WEEKS COUNT`
#ASSERT `s 2G -- what does this break do to my service` `other leave my employer allowed` FALSE 0 `ANY DAY` TRUE `ANY DAY` `ANY DAY` EQUALS `KEPT, NOT COUNTED`
-- Work injury (Fiona, 1 August to 1 December 1999).
#ASSERT `s 2G -- what does this break do to my service` `absence because of an injury arising out of or in the course of my employment` FALSE 0 (`on` 1 8 1999) TRUE (`on` 1 12 1999) (`on` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `KEPT, NOT COUNTED`
#ASSERT `s 2G -- what does this break do to my service` `my employer interrupting or ending my service intending to avoid granting long service leave` FALSE 0 `ANY DAY` FALSE `ANY DAY` `ANY DAY` EQUALS `KEPT, COUNTS`
#ASSERT `s 2G -- what does this break do to my service` `serving in the Defence Force, other than continuous full-time service` FALSE 0 `ANY DAY` TRUE `ANY DAY` `ANY DAY` EQUALS `KEPT, COUNTS`
#ASSERT `s 2G -- what does this break do to my service` `working for my employer temporarily outside the ACT` FALSE 0 `ANY DAY` TRUE `ANY DAY` `ANY DAY` EQUALS `KEPT, COUNTS`
-- Seasonal break of 5 months: s 2G (3) keeps continuity whatever the length.
#ASSERT `s 2G -- what does this break do to my service` `a break caused by the seasonal nature of the work` FALSE 0 (`on` 1 5 2026) TRUE (`on` 1 10 2026) (`on` 1 11 2026) EQUALS `KEPT, NOT COUNTED`
-- Fiona resigns 31 December 1994 and comes back 1 February 1995: within 2 months.
#ASSERT `s 2G -- what does this break do to my service` `OTHER BREAK` FALSE 0 (`on` 1 1 1995) TRUE (`on` 1 2 1995) (`on` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `KEPT, NOT COUNTED`
-- Any other break from 1 January 2026: 2 months after is 1 March 2026.
#ASSERT `s 2G -- what does this break do to my service` `OTHER BREAK` FALSE 0 (`on` 1 1 2026) TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) (`on` 1 4 2026) EQUALS `KEPT, NOT COUNTED`
#ASSERT `s 2G -- what does this break do to my service` `OTHER BREAK` FALSE 0 (`on` 1 1 2026) TRUE (`on` 2 3 2026) (`on` 1 4 2026) EQUALS `BROKEN`
#ASSERT `s 2G -- what does this break do to my service` `OTHER BREAK` FALSE 0 (`on` 1 1 2026) FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `NOT KNOWN YET`
#ASSERT `s 2G -- what does this break do to my service` `OTHER BREAK` FALSE 0 (`on` 1 1 2026) FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 2 3 2026) EQUALS `BROKEN`

§ `ss 10, 10A, 11 -- earlier service`

#ASSERT `ss 10, 10A, 11 -- does my earlier service count` `the business was transmitted to my present employer, and I went straight from the old employer to the new one` `ANY DAY` `ANY DAY` EQUALS `yes: your service is not interrupted by the transmission, and your service with the first employer is service with the second (s 10)`
#ASSERT `ss 10, 10A, 11 -- does my earlier service count` `my present employer took over a services contract from my old employer, under a contract obliging it to employ the old contractor's staff where practicable, and employed me under that obligation` `ANY DAY` `ANY DAY` EQUALS `yes: your service for the first contractor and the second contractor is taken to be 1 period of service for the second contractor (s 10A)`
#ASSERT `ss 10, 10A, 11 -- does my earlier service count` `I worked over a continuous period for two or more companies that are all associated companies (subsidiaries, holding companies or related bodies corporate)` `ANY DAY` `ANY DAY` EQUALS `yes: you are entitled as if you had been employed throughout by the company employing you when your leave accrues (s 11)`
-- Apprenticeship ended 30 June 2025: service begun on 30 June 2026 is within 1 year; 1 July 2026 is not.
#ASSERT `ss 10, 10A, 11 -- does my earlier service count` `I was an apprentice or under an approved training contract with my present employer` (`on` 30 6 2025) (`on` 30 6 2026) EQUALS `yes: the apprenticeship or training contract is part of your continuous service, because you began service within 1 year after it ended (dictionary, continuous service (d))`
#ASSERT `ss 10, 10A, 11 -- does my earlier service count` `I was an apprentice or under an approved training contract with my present employer` (`on` 30 6 2025) (`on` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `the apprenticeship or training contract is not brought in by the dictionary, because you did not begin service within 1 year after it ended; the Act says nothing more (NOTHING-kind)`
#ASSERT `ss 10, 10A, 11 -- does my earlier service count` `I worked for a different, unconnected employer` `ANY DAY` `ANY DAY` EQUALS `no: a period of service is continuous service with a particular employer; service with an unconnected employer is not part of it (the text's no, s 2G (1))`

§ `ss 3, 4 -- entitlement`

-- The Act's own example (s 2G): Fiona starts 1 January 1992; 9 months not counted; "Her 10 years long service leave
-- falls due on 1 October 2002."
#ASSERT `the day` 10 `years of service are completed from` (`on` 1 1 1992) 9 0 EQUALS `on` 1 10 2002
-- 7 years from 1 January 2019, nothing uncounted: 1 January 2026.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- the day I become entitled to long service leave` (`on` 1 1 2019) 0 0 EQUALS `on` 1 1 2026
-- With 2 months and 10 days uncounted: 1 March 2026, then 10 days on, 11 March 2026.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- the day I become entitled to long service leave` (`on` 1 1 2019) 2 10 EQUALS `on` 11 3 2026
-- Started 29 February 2020: 2027 has no 29 February, so the last day of February (fork F1).
#ASSERT `s 3 -- the day I become entitled to long service leave` (`on` 29 2 2020) 0 0 EQUALS `on` 28 2 2027
-- Whole years completed: the day before the 7th anniversary, and the day.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- how many years of service have I completed` (`on` 1 1 2019) 0 0 (`on` 31 12 2025) EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `s 3 -- how many years of service have I completed` (`on` 1 1 2019) 0 0 (`on` 1 1 2026) EQUALS 7
-- With 2 months and 10 days uncounted the 7th year ends on 11 March 2026 (agreeing with the s 3 day above).
#ASSERT `s 3 -- how many years of service have I completed` (`on` 1 1 2019) 2 10 (`on` 10 3 2026) EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `s 3 -- how many years of service have I completed` (`on` 1 1 2019) 2 10 (`on` 11 3 2026) EQUALS 7
-- Months of leave: 10 years 2 months; 9 years 1.8; 7 years 1.4; 6 years none.
#ASSERT `s 4 -- how many months of long service leave am I entitled to` (`on` 1 1 2016) 0 0 (`on` 1 1 2026) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `s 4 -- how many months of long service leave am I entitled to` (`on` 1 1 2016) 0 0 (`on` 31 12 2025) EQUALS (9 DIVIDED BY 5)
#ASSERT `s 4 -- how many months of long service leave am I entitled to` (`on` 1 1 2019) 0 0 (`on` 1 1 2026) EQUALS (7 DIVIDED BY 5)
#ASSERT `s 4 -- how many months of long service leave am I entitled to` (`on` 1 1 2019) 0 0 (`on` 31 12 2025) EQUALS 0

§ `ss 2D, 2E, 2EA -- portable schemes`

#ASSERT `ss 2D, 2E, 2EA -- does a portable scheme affect my claim` `none` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no effect: these sections deal only with employees registered under a portable scheme who elected to take its benefits; this Act applies to you as usual (NOTHING-kind)`
#ASSERT `ss 2D, 2E, 2EA -- does a portable scheme affect my claim` `the building and construction industry scheme (Long Service Leave (Building and Construction Industry) Act 1981)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `your election under the portable scheme does not stop you receiving benefits under this Act (ss 2D (2), 2E (2), 2EA (2))`
#ASSERT `ss 2D, 2E, 2EA -- does a portable scheme affect my claim` `the contract cleaning industry scheme (Long Service Leave (Contract Cleaning Industry) Act 1999)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: you are not entitled to a benefit under this Act for a period for which you received a benefit under the portable scheme (the text's no, ss 2D (3), 2E (3), 2EA (3))`
#ASSERT `ss 2D, 2E, 2EA -- does a portable scheme affect my claim` `a scheme under the Long Service Leave (Portable Schemes) Act 2009` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no effect: these sections deal only with employees registered under a portable scheme who elected to take its benefits; this Act applies to you as usual (NOTHING-kind)`

§ `s 6 (1) -- granting leave`

#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my employer grant my leave` 6 0 FALSE EQUALS `not yet: you have not completed 7 years of service, so you are not yet entitled to long service leave (s 3 (1))`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my employer grant my leave` 7 0 FALSE EQUALS `yes, as soon as practicable after you became entitled, having regard to the needs of your employer's business (s 6 (1) (b) (i)); not granting it is an offence (50 penalty units)`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my employer grant my leave` 7 0 TRUE EQUALS `yes, at the time or times you and your employer agreed (s 6 (1) (b) (ii)); not granting it then is an offence (50 penalty units)`
-- 10 years (2 months), 1.2 taken: 0.8 month left, under 28/31.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my employer grant my leave` 10 1.2 FALSE EQUALS `s 6 (1) puts no duty on your employer: your untaken leave is less than 4 weeks, and the Act says nothing about when shorter leave must be granted (NOTHING-kind)`
-- 8 years (1.6 months), 1.4 taken: 0.2 left.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my employer grant my leave` 8 1.4 FALSE EQUALS `s 6 (1) puts no duty on your employer: your untaken leave is less than 4 weeks, and the Act says nothing about when shorter leave must be granted (NOTHING-kind)`
-- 10 years, 1.05 taken: 0.95 left, between 28/31 (0.903) and 1.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my employer grant my leave` 10 1.05 FALSE EQUALS `it depends on the length of the month: your untaken leave is between 28/31 of a month and 1 month, and the Act does not say how a month of leave converts to weeks (NOTHING-kind)`
-- 10 years, 1 taken: exactly 1 month left, always 4 weeks or more.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my employer grant my leave` 10 1 FALSE EQUALS `yes, as soon as practicable after you became entitled, having regard to the needs of your employer's business (s 6 (1) (b) (i)); not granting it is an offence (50 penalty units)`

§ `s 6 (2) -- 60 days' written notice`

-- Leave from 1 March 2027: 60 days before is 31 December 2026 (28 days of February, 31 of January, 1 of December).
#ASSERT `s 6 (2) -- the last day for written notice of my leave` (`on` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `on` 31 12 2026
#ASSERT `s 6 (2) -- did I get enough notice of my leave` (`on` 1 3 2027) TRUE FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 1 2 2027) EQUALS `s 6 (2) does not apply: you agreed otherwise (s 6 (3))`
-- Notice on the last day, and a day late.
#ASSERT `s 6 (2) -- did I get enough notice of my leave` (`on` 1 3 2027) FALSE TRUE (`on` 31 12 2026) (`on` 1 2 2027) EQUALS `enough notice: your employer gave you written notice at least 60 days before your leave starts (s 6 (2))`
#ASSERT `s 6 (2) -- did I get enough notice of my leave` (`on` 1 3 2027) FALSE TRUE (`on` 1 1 2027) (`on` 1 2 2027) EQUALS `not enough notice: written notice came less than 60 days before your leave starts; that is an offence by your employer (the text's no, s 6 (2), 50 penalty units)`
#ASSERT `s 6 (2) -- did I get enough notice of my leave` (`on` 1 3 2027) FALSE TRUE (`on` 1 10 2026) (`on` 1 2 2027) EQUALS `enough notice: your employer gave you written notice at least 60 days before your leave starts (s 6 (2))`
-- No notice yet: on the last day there is still time; the day after there is not.
#ASSERT `s 6 (2) -- did I get enough notice of my leave` (`on` 1 3 2027) FALSE FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 31 12 2026) EQUALS `no written notice yet, and there is still time for 60 days' notice`
#ASSERT `s 6 (2) -- did I get enough notice of my leave` (`on` 1 3 2027) FALSE FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 1 1 2027) EQUALS `no written notice, and it is now too late for 60 days' notice: that is an offence by your employer (s 6 (2), 50 penalty units)`

§ `s 7 -- the weekly rate`

#ASSERT `s 7 -- my weekly rate of pay for long service leave` `full-time` 1500 0 0 0 EQUALS 1500
-- Part-time, 20 hours a week on average at 40 an hour: 800.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- my weekly rate of pay for long service leave` `part-time or casual` 0 20 40 0 EQUALS 800
-- Moved to part-time within 2 years: 390,000 over 5 years / 5 = 78,000 a year; / 52 = 1,500 a week.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- my weekly rate of pay for long service leave` `part-time or casual, after working full-time within the 2 years before I became entitled` 0 20 40 390000 EQUALS 1500

§ `s 8 -- manner of payment`

#ASSERT `s 8 -- is the way I am paid for my leave allowed` `in advance, for the whole period of the leave` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: payment in advance for the whole period (s 8 (1) (a))`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- is the way I am paid for my leave allowed` `at my usual pay times, as if I were working` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: payment at your usual pay times (s 8 (1) (b))`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- is the way I am paid for my leave allowed` `at my usual pay times, as if I were working` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: payment at your usual pay times (s 8 (1) (b))`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- is the way I am paid for my leave allowed` `at my usual pay times, as if I were working` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: you asked to be paid by cheque posted to an address you nominated, and that was not done; that is an offence by your employer (the text's no, s 8 (1) (b), 50 penalty units)`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- is the way I am paid for my leave allowed` `in another way I agreed with my employer` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: payment in a way you and your employer agreed (s 8 (1) (c))`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- is the way I am paid for my leave allowed` `in another way I did not agree to` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: payment for long service leave must be in advance, at your usual pay times, or as you agree; anything else is an offence by your employer (the text's no, s 8 (1), 50 penalty units)`
#ASSERT `s 8 (3) -- when do I get a pay rise during my leave` `in advance, for the whole period of the leave` FALSE EQUALS `as soon as practicable when your leave ends (s 8 (3) (a))`
#ASSERT `s 8 (3) -- when do I get a pay rise during my leave` `at my usual pay times, as if I were working` FALSE EQUALS `at your usual pay times, as the rest of your leave pay (s 8 (3) (b))`
#ASSERT `s 8 (3) -- when do I get a pay rise during my leave` `in another way I agreed with my employer` TRUE EQUALS `as you and your employer agreed (s 8 (3) (c))`
#ASSERT `s 8 (3) -- when do I get a pay rise during my leave` `in another way I agreed with my employer` FALSE EQUALS `as soon as practicable when your leave ends, since you and your employer have not agreed how (s 8 (3) (c))`
#ASSERT `s 8 (3) -- when do I get a pay rise during my leave` `in another way I did not agree to` FALSE EQUALS `s 8 (3) covers only payment made in a way s 8 (1) allows; the Act says nothing about a rise paid with leave paid some other way (NOTHING-kind)`

§ `s 9 -- holidays`

#ASSERT `s 9 -- how many days is my leave extended for holidays` 2 1 EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `s 9 -- how many days is my leave extended for holidays` 0 0 EQUALS 0

§ `s 11A -- untaken leave when employment ends`

-- 10 years, nothing taken, 1,200 a week: 2 months x 52/12 weeks x 1,200 = 2 x 5,200 = 10,400.
#ASSERT `s 11A -- how much am I owed for untaken leave when my employment ends` 10 0 `FT` 1200 0 0 EQUALS 10400
-- 7 years: 1.4 x 5,200 = 7,280.
#ASSERT `s 11A -- how much am I owed for untaken leave when my employment ends` 7 0 `FT` 1200 0 0 EQUALS 7280
-- 10 years, all 2 months taken: nothing.
#ASSERT `s 11A -- how much am I owed for untaken leave when my employment ends` 10 2 `FT` 1200 0 0 EQUALS 0
-- 6 years: no credit (fork F4).
#ASSERT `s 11A -- how much am I owed for untaken leave when my employment ends` 6 0 `FT` 1200 0 0 EQUALS 0
-- Part-time at the end, 20 hours at 60 = 1,200 a week; 10 years, 0.5 taken: 1.5 x 5,200 = 7,800.
#ASSERT `s 11A -- how much am I owed for untaken leave when my employment ends` 10 0.5 `PT` 0 20 60 EQUALS 7800
-- 12 years (2.4 months), 1.4 taken: 1 month x 52/12 x 1,500 = 6,500.
#ASSERT `s 11A -- how much am I owed for untaken leave when my employment ends` 12 1.4 `FT` 1500 0 0 EQUALS 6500

-- Ended 1 January 2026: 90 days after is 1 April 2026 (31 + 28 + 31).
#ASSERT `s 11A (4) -- the last day for payment of my leave credit` (`on` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `on` 1 4 2026
#ASSERT `s 11A (4) -- was my leave credit paid in time` FALSE (`on` 1 1 2026) FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `s 11A does not apply: you had no long service leave credit when the employment ended (the text's no, s 11A (2) (b))`
#ASSERT `s 11A (4) -- was my leave credit paid in time` TRUE (`on` 1 1 2026) TRUE (`on` 1 4 2026) (`on` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `paid in time: within 90 days after your employment ended (s 11A (4))`
#ASSERT `s 11A (4) -- was my leave credit paid in time` TRUE (`on` 1 1 2026) TRUE (`on` 2 4 2026) (`on` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `paid late: more than 90 days after your employment ended; that is an offence by your employer (s 11A (4), 50 penalty units), and the amount was owed all along`
#ASSERT `s 11A (4) -- was my leave credit paid in time` TRUE (`on` 1 1 2026) FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 1 4 2026) EQUALS `not paid yet, and the 90 days have not run out`
#ASSERT `s 11A (4) -- was my leave credit paid in time` TRUE (`on` 1 1 2026) FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 2 4 2026) EQUALS `not paid, and the 90 days have run out: that is an offence by your employer (s 11A (4), 50 penalty units); you are still owed the amount`

§ `s 11C -- pro rata`

#ASSERT `s 11C -- am I owed pro rata long service leave pay` 7 `ILLNESS` FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `s 11C does not apply because you had completed 7 years: you are owed payment for your untaken leave under s 11A instead`
#ASSERT `s 11C -- am I owed pro rata long service leave pay` 4 `ILLNESS` FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `no: s 11C needs at least 5 years of service (the text's no, s 11C (1) (b))`
#ASSERT `s 11C -- am I owed pro rata long service leave pay` 5 `ILLNESS` FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `PRO RATA YES`
#ASSERT `s 11C -- am I owed pro rata long service leave pay` 6 `NECESSITY` TRUE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `PRO RATA YES`
#ASSERT `s 11C -- am I owed pro rata long service leave pay` 6 `NECESSITY` FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `PRO RATA NOT A LISTED WAY`
-- Retiring: 64 and 65 with no award age; 60 where an award fixes 60.
#ASSERT `s 11C -- am I owed pro rata long service leave pay` 6 `OTHER REASON` FALSE 64 FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `PRO RATA NOT A LISTED WAY`
#ASSERT `s 11C -- am I owed pro rata long service leave pay` 6 `OTHER REASON` FALSE 65 FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `PRO RATA YES`
#ASSERT `s 11C -- am I owed pro rata long service leave pay` 6 `OTHER REASON` FALSE 60 TRUE 60 FALSE EQUALS `PRO RATA YES`
#ASSERT `s 11C -- am I owed pro rata long service leave pay` 6 `OTHER REASON` FALSE 59 TRUE 60 FALSE EQUALS `PRO RATA NOT A LISTED WAY`
#ASSERT `s 11C -- am I owed pro rata long service leave pay` 6 `DIED` FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `PRO RATA YES`
#ASSERT `s 11C -- am I owed pro rata long service leave pay` 6 `DISMISSED` FALSE 0 FALSE 0 TRUE EQUALS `PRO RATA NOT A LISTED WAY`
#ASSERT `s 11C -- am I owed pro rata long service leave pay` 6 `DISMISSED` FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `PRO RATA YES`

-- Started 1 January 2020, full-time at 1,200 a week (5,200 a month of leave at 52/12 weeks).
-- 72 months (ended 1 January 2026): 72/120 x 2 = 1.2 months x 5,200 = 6,240.
#ASSERT `s 11C -- how much pro rata long service leave pay am I owed` (`on` 1 1 2020) 0 0 (`on` 1 1 2026) `ILLNESS` FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE `FT` 1200 0 0 EQUALS 6240
-- 60 months (ended 1 January 2025): 1 month = 5,200. 59 months (ended 31 December 2024): nothing.
#ASSERT `s 11C -- how much pro rata long service leave pay am I owed` (`on` 1 1 2020) 0 0 (`on` 1 1 2025) `ILLNESS` FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE `FT` 1200 0 0 EQUALS 5200
#ASSERT `s 11C -- how much pro rata long service leave pay am I owed` (`on` 1 1 2020) 0 0 (`on` 31 12 2024) `ILLNESS` FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE `FT` 1200 0 0 EQUALS 0
-- 83 months (ended 31 December 2026): 83/60 x 5,200 = 431,600/60 = 21,580/3.
#ASSERT `s 11C -- how much pro rata long service leave pay am I owed` (`on` 1 1 2020) 0 0 (`on` 31 12 2026) `ILLNESS` FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE `FT` 1200 0 0 EQUALS (21580 DIVIDED BY 3)
-- 84 months (ended 1 January 2027): 7 years, s 11A territory, nothing under s 11C.
#ASSERT `s 11C -- how much pro rata long service leave pay am I owed` (`on` 1 1 2020) 0 0 (`on` 1 1 2027) `ILLNESS` FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE `FT` 1200 0 0 EQUALS 0
-- Dismissed for serious and wilful misconduct at 72 months: nothing.
#ASSERT `s 11C -- how much pro rata long service leave pay am I owed` (`on` 1 1 2020) 0 0 (`on` 1 1 2026) `DISMISSED` FALSE 0 FALSE 0 TRUE `FT` 1200 0 0 EQUALS 0
-- Part-time at the end, 25 hours at 40 = 1,000 a week; 72 months: 1.2 x 52/12 x 1,000 = 5,200.
#ASSERT `s 11C -- how much pro rata long service leave pay am I owed` (`on` 1 1 2020) 0 0 (`on` 1 1 2026) `DIED` FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE `PT` 0 25 40 EQUALS 5200
-- 6 months not counted: 72 - 6 = 66 months at 1 January 2026: 66/60 x 5,200 = 5,720.
#ASSERT `s 11C -- how much pro rata long service leave pay am I owed` (`on` 1 1 2020) 6 0 (`on` 1 1 2026) `ILLNESS` FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE `FT` 1200 0 0 EQUALS 5720

§ `s 12 (2) -- records`

#ASSERT `s 12 (2) -- until when must my employer keep my records` FALSE (`on` 15 3 2026) `ANY DAY` EQUALS `on` 15 3 2033
-- Death; amounts paid on 29 February 2028: 7 years on, 2035 has no 29 February (fork F1).
#ASSERT `s 12 (2) -- until when must my employer keep my records` TRUE (`on` 1 1 2028) (`on` 29 2 2028) EQUALS `on` 28 2 2035

§ `ss 13D, 13E -- complaints`

#ASSERT `s 13D -- can someone represent me at the conference` TRUE EQUALS `yes: the authorised officer has consented (s 13D (4))`
#ASSERT `s 13D -- can someone represent me at the conference` FALSE EQUALS `no: an individual is not entitled to be represented at the conference by another person without the authorised officer's consent (the text's no, s 13D (4) (a))`
-- Received 1 February 2026: 28 days after is 1 March 2026.
#ASSERT `s 13E -- did my employer comply with the notice in time` (`on` 1 2 2026) TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) (`on` 1 4 2026) EQUALS `complied in time: within 28 days after it received the notice (s 13E (1))`
#ASSERT `s 13E -- did my employer comply with the notice in time` (`on` 1 2 2026) TRUE (`on` 2 3 2026) (`on` 1 4 2026) EQUALS `complied late: more than 28 days after it received the notice; that is an offence (s 13E (2), 50 penalty units)`
#ASSERT `s 13E -- did my employer comply with the notice in time` (`on` 1 2 2026) FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `not complied yet, and the 28 days have not run out`
#ASSERT `s 13E -- did my employer comply with the notice in time` (`on` 1 2 2026) FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 2 3 2026) EQUALS `not complied, and the 28 days have run out: that is an offence by your employer (s 13E (2), 50 penalty units)`

§ `s 14 -- awards and agreements`

#ASSERT `s 14 -- does my award or agreement change my long service leave` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `there is no award or agreement on the point: the Act applies (s 14 (1))`
#ASSERT `s 14 -- does my award or agreement change my long service leave` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the award or agreement's more advantageous rights stand (s 14 (2))`
#ASSERT `s 14 -- does my award or agreement change my long service leave` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the Act has effect despite an award or agreement to the contrary (the text's no, s 14 (1))`
